  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "The graph of a linear function passes through \\((-2,0)\\) and \\((0,4)\\). Its equation is ( ).",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(y=-2x+4\\)",
    "B": "\\(y=2x-4\\)",
    "C": "\\(y=4x+2\\)",
    "D": "\\(y=2x+4\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Passing through \\((0,4)\\) gives \\(b=4\\). Substituting \\((-2,0)\\) gives \\(-2k+4=0\\), so \\(k=2\\). Therefore, \\(y=2x+4\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Test the choices\n\nThe point \\((0,4)\\) requires the constant term to be \\(4\\), so only A and D remain. At \\(x=-2\\), A gives \\(y=-2(-2)+4=8\\), while D gives \\(y=2(-2)+4=0\\). Thus D passes through both given points. Since two distinct points determine a line, the equation is \\(y=2x+4\\), choice D.",
